:"1635290115.197600","team":"T03C4RC8V","replace_original":false,"delete_original":false,"blocks":[{"type":"rich_text","block_id":"=pa"}]},{"client_msg_id":"6444dd24-603b-4716-82cd-4765bf007a70","type":"message","user":"U01AQ5BFNLX","text":"\u003c@U8996GYBF\u003e 突然すいません。`next/image`を使ったときに個別にスタイルかけたいことがあると思うんですがこういう時どうしてますか?","ts":"1635290082.196500","team":"T03C4RC8V","replace_original":false,"delete_original":false,"blocks":[{"type":"rich_text","block_id":"+/p"}]},{"client_msg_id":"2368360e-0a7e-431b-88e7-9ac44f2f9d49","type":"message","user":"U8996GYBF","text":"似てる？のだと \u003chttps://eslint.org/docs/rules/no-await-in-loop\u003e とか","ts":"1635289868.195200","attachments":[{"fallback":"ESLint - Pluggable JavaScript linter: no-await-in-loop - Rules","id":1,"title":"no-await-in-loop - Rules","title_link":"https://eslint.org/docs/rules/no-await-in-loop","text":"A pluggable and configurable linter tool for identifying and reporting on patterns in JavaScript. Maintain your code quality with ease.","thumb_url":"https://eslint.org/assets/img/favicon.512x512.png","blocks":null,"service_name":"ESLint - Pluggable JavaScript linter","service_icon":"https://eslint.org/assets/img/favicon.512x512.png","thumb_width":512,"thumb_height":512,"from_url":"https://eslint.org/docs/rules/no-await-in-loop","original_url":"https://eslint.org/docs/rules/no-await-in-loop"}],"team":"T03C4RC8V","replace_original":false,"delete_original":false,"blocks":[{"type":"rich_text","block_id":"VXafQ"}]},{"client_msg_id":"1696ca61-b573-4e8a-82da-8a7bb20d3c77","type":"message","user":"U8996GYBF","text":"\u003chttps://github.com/typescript-eslint/typescript-eslint/blob/master/packages/eslint-plugin/docs/rules/no-floating-promises.md\u003e","ts":"1635289809.194700","attachments":[{"color":"24292f","fallback":"\u003chttps://github.com/typescript-eslint/typescript-eslint/blob/master/packages/eslint-plugin/docs/rules/no-floating-promises.md | no-floating-promises.md\u003e","id":1,"title":"\u003chttps://github.com/typescript-eslint/typescript-eslint/blob/master/packages/eslint-plugin/docs/rules/no-floating-promises.md | no-floating-promises.md\u003e","text":"*Requires Promise-like values to be handled appropriately (`no-floating-promises`)*\n\nThis rule forbids usage of Promise-like values in statements without handling  \ntheir errors appropriately. Unhandled promises can cause several issues, such  \nas improperly sequenced operations, ignored Promise rejections and more. Valid  \nways of handling a Promise-valued statement include `await`ing, returning, and  \neither calling `.then()` with two arguments or `.catch()` with one argument.\n\n*Rule Details*\n\nExamples of *incorrect* code for this rule:\n\n```\nconst promise = new Promise((resolve, reject) =\u0026gt; resolve('value'));\npromise;\n\nasync function returnsPromise() {\n  return 'value';\n}\nreturnsPromise().then(() =\u0026gt; {});\n\nPromise.reject('value').catch();\n\nPromise.reject('value').finally();\n```\n\nExamples of *correct* code for this rule:\n\n```\nconst promise = new Promise((resolve, reject) =\u0026gt; resolve('value'));\nawait promise;\n\nasync function returnsPromise() {\n  return 'value';\n}\nreturnsPromise().then(\n  () =\u0026gt; {},\n  () =\u0026gt; {},\n);\n\nPromise.reject('value').catch(() =\u0026gt; {});\n\nPromise.reject('value').finally(() =\u0026gt; {});\n```\n\n*Options*\n\nThe rule accepts an options object with the following properties:\n\n```\ntype Options = {\n  // if true, checking void expressions will be skipped\n  ignoreVoid?: boolean;\n  // if true, checking for async iife will be skipped\n  ignoreIIFE?: boolean;\n};\n\nconst defaults = {\n  ignoreVoid: true,\n  ignoreIIFE: false,\n};\n```\n\n*`ignoreVoid`*\n\nThis allows you to stop the rule reporting promises consumed with void operator.  \nThis can be a good way to explicitly mark a promise as intentionally not awaited.\n\nExamples of *correct* code for this rule with `{ ignoreVoid: true }`:\n\n```\nasync function returnsPromise() {\n  return 'value';\n}\nvoid returnsPromise();\n\nvoid Promise.reject('value');\n```\n\nWith this option set to `true`, and if you are using `no-void`, you should turn on the \u003chttps://eslint.org/docs/rules/no-void#allowasstatement|`allowAsStatement`\u003e option.\n\n*`ignoreIIFE`*\n\nThis allows you to skip checking of async iife\n\nExamples of *correct* code for this rule with `{ ignoreIIFE: true }`:\n\n```\nawait(async function () {\n  await res(1);\n})();\n\n(async function () {\n  await res(1);\n})();\n```\n\n*When Not To Use It*\n\nIf you do not use Promise-like values in your codebase, or want to allow them to remain unhandled.\n\n*Related to*\n\n• TSLint: \u003chttps://palantir.github.io/tslint/rules/no-floating-promises/|'no-floating-promises'\u003e\n\n*Attributes*\n\n☑︎ :white_check_mark: Recommended\n☐ :wrench: Fixable\n☑︎ :thought_balloon: Requires type information","mrkdwn_in":["text"],"blocks":null,"footer":"\u003chttps://github.com/typescript-eslint/typescript-eslint|typescript-eslint/typescript-eslint\u003e","footer_icon":"https://slack.github.com/static/img/favicon-neutral.png"}],"team":"T03C4RC8V","replace_original":false,"delete_original":false,"blocks":[{"type":"rich_text","block_id":"iny"}]},{"client_msg_id":"d3737734-a3d2-41cf-97c6-40172b47306a","type":"message","user":"U9S4G0LJW","text":"便利","ts":"1635289716.194500","team":"T03C4RC8V","replace_original":false,"delete_original":false,"blocks":[{"type":"rich_text","block_id":"NsLK"}]},{"client_msg_id":"146E1268-E706-402B-9A84-F2A7EB863203","type":"message","user":"U8996GYBF","text":"ありがちなヒューマンエラーほんとに全部潰れる","ts":"1635289712.194300","team":"T03C4RC8V","replace_original":false,"delete_original":false,"blocks":[{"type":"rich_text","block_id":"rPD"}]},{"client_msg_id":"20D9BD26-1A9A-4863-A785-EC4B2077CA5D","type":"message","user":"U8996GYBF","text":"ガチガチにしたeslintは本当にめっちゃ強いですよ","ts":"1635289698.193700","team":"T03C4RC8V","replace_original":false,"delete_original":false,"blocks":[{"typ